---
import ServiceLayout from '../../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
---

<ServiceLayout
  serviceName="InSinkErator Installation & Repair"
  serviceSlug="insinkerator"
  heroTitle="InSinkErator Installation & Repair — Brisbane, Logan & Gold Coast"
  heroSubtitle="Licensed plumbers for InSinkErator food waste disposer installation, replacement and repairs across South-East Queensland. Upfront pricing, same-day service, QBCC licensed."
  heroImage="/images/insinkerator-hero.png"

  keyBenefits={[
    'Same-day installation and repair across Brisbane, Logan, Gold Coast and Ipswich',
    'QBCC licensed plumbers — your warranty stays valid and your plumbing is compliant',
    'Upfront pricing before we start — no hidden call-out fees, no surprises',
    'We supply InSinkErator units or install your own — all models and configurations',
  ]}

  process={[
    {
      title: 'Assess your sink and under-sink plumbing',
      description: 'We check the sink opening, flange compatibility, available cabinet space, existing waste trap, drainage connection and dishwasher inlet. We confirm whether the selected unit suits your setup before any work begins.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Provide upfront options and pricing',
      description: 'We explain the required plumbing work, present clear options and confirm the price before we start. If we are supplying the unit, we advise on the right InSinkErator model for your household size and usage.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Complete the installation or repair',
      description: 'We connect the unit to the sink waste, configure the trap and drainage connections, reconnect the dishwasher drain where applicable, and complete all required plumbing work under the sink.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Test, check and hand over',
      description: 'We run the unit with cold water, check all accessible connections for leaks, confirm the drain is flowing correctly, and walk you through correct operation — including what to put in and what to avoid.',
    },
  ]}

  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'Do I need a licensed plumber to install an InSinkErator in Queensland?',
      a: 'Yes. Under the Plumbing and Drainage Act 2018 (Qld) and the Standard Plumbing and Drainage Regulation 2019, all plumbing connection work — including connecting a food waste disposer to your sink waste and drainage — must be carried out by a QBCC-licensed plumber. DIY plumbing connections can void your InSinkErator warranty, create drainage problems, and result in compliance issues if you sell or lease the property. Pulse Plumbing, Gas & Civil holds QBCC Contractor Licence 15384771.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What InSinkErator models do you install?',
      a: 'We install all InSinkErator models available in Australia, including the Badger, Evolution and Essential series. Popular models we regularly install include the InSinkErator Badger 5, Evolution Compact, Evolution Excel and the Evolution 200. We can advise on the right model for your household — a 2-person household typically suits a Badger or Essential series unit, while larger families or those who cook frequently benefit from an Evolution model with a larger grinding chamber.',
    },
    {
      q: 'How much does InSinkErator installation cost in Brisbane?',
      a: 'InSinkErator installation by a licensed plumber in Brisbane and South-East Queensland typically costs between $150 and $350 for the labour component, depending on the complexity of the under-sink plumbing, whether the dishwasher drain needs reconnecting, and whether any adjustments to the existing waste trap are required. If you are supplying your own unit, we charge for labour only. If we are supplying the unit, the cost of the InSinkErator is additional. We provide an upfront price before starting — call 0452 188 420 or 07 2150 4175 for a same-day quote.',
    },
    {
      q: 'My InSinkErator is jammed — what should I try first?',
      a: 'A jammed InSinkErator is usually caused by a hard object (a spoon, bone or fruit pit) lodged in the grinding chamber. First, turn off the power at the wall switch. Locate the self-service wrenchette (a small hex key in a plastic sleeve attached to the base of the unit) and insert it into the centre hole on the bottom of the unit. Work it back and forth until the grinding plate spins freely. Use tongs — never your hand — to remove any object from inside the unit. Press the red reset button on the base of the unit, restore power and test with cold water running. If the unit still does not operate, call Pulse on 0452 188 420.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Why is my InSinkErator leaking?',
      a: 'InSinkErator leaks typically come from one of three places: the sink flange (where the unit mounts to the sink — usually a failed putty seal), the side discharge outlet (where the waste pipe connects — usually a loose connection or worn seal), or the bottom of the unit (which indicates an internal seal failure and usually means the unit needs replacing). Leaks under the sink can damage your cabinetry quickly — call Pulse on 0452 188 420 for a same-day assessment.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What food waste can I put in an InSinkErator?',
      a: 'InSinkErator units are designed for most natural food scraps: vegetable peelings, fruit peelings and pits, eggshells, coffee grounds, tea leaves, meat scraps, fish bones, prawn shells, pasta and rice. Always use cold water — not hot — when operating the unit, and keep the water running for 10–15 seconds after grinding is complete to flush the drain. Do not put fats, oils, grease, fibrous vegetables (celery, corn husks), large bones, oyster shells, glass, metal or non-food items into the unit.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can an InSinkErator cause a blocked drain?',
      a: 'An InSinkErator can contribute to a blocked drain if the wrong items are put through it, if insufficient cold water is used during operation, or if the downstream pipework already has grease build-up. If your sink is slow to drain or backing up after using the InSinkErator, the issue is likely in the waste trap or further down the drain line — not the unit itself. Pulse can diagnose and clear the blockage using CCTV inspection and high-pressure water jetting.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do you repair InSinkErator units or just replace them?',
      a: 'We handle all plumbing-related repairs: leaking flanges, worn seals, loose waste connections, blocked traps and drainage issues. Internal electrical or motor faults are outside the scope of plumbing work and require the manufacturer or an electrician. For older units (7+ years) with internal faults, replacement is usually more cost-effective than repair — we will give you an honest assessment and a clear price for both options.',
    },
    {
      q: 'How long does InSinkErator installation take?',
      a: 'A straightforward replacement of an existing unit typically takes 30–60 minutes. A first-time installation where the sink waste and trap need to be reconfigured can take 1–2 hours. We aim to leave your kitchen clean and fully operational on the same visit.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What areas do you service for InSinkErator installation?',
      a: 'We install and repair InSinkErator units across South-East Queensland including Brisbane (south), Logan City, Redland City, Ormeau, Beenleigh, Coomera, Pimpama, Upper Coomera, Oxenford, Helensvale, Nerang, Robina, Mudgeeraba, Burleigh Heads, Palm Beach, Southport, Ipswich and surrounding suburbs. Call 0452 188 420 to confirm availability in your suburb.',
    },
  ]}

  relatedIndustries={[
    'property-management',
    'commercial-real-estate',
    'new-builds',
    'retail',
    'aged-care',
  ]}

  metaTitle="InSinkErator Installation & Repair Brisbane, Logan & Gold Coast | Pulse Plumbing"
  metaDescription="QBCC licensed InSinkErator installation and repair across Brisbane, Logan, Gold Coast and Ipswich. Same-day service, upfront pricing. Call 0452 188 420."
>

  <!-- ── Price Promise offer card — renders above FAQ via named slot ── -->
  <div slot="offer" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto my-10 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="bg-[#0172ae] text-white rounded-2xl px-8 py-10">

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">InSinkErator Installation — Pulse Price Promise</h2>

      <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
        {[
          'Upfront price confirmed before we start — no surprises on the invoice',
          'Same-day installation available across Brisbane, Logan and Gold Coast',
          'We supply the unit or install yours — all InSinkErator models',
        ].map((point) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#10a2d5] flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd"/>
            </svg>
            {point}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <p class="text-sm opacity-80 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
        All plumbing work carried out by QBCC-licensed plumbers. Lic 15384771.<br />
        Pricing subject to on-site assessment. Call for a same-day quote.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
        <a
          href="tel:0452188420"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-white text-[#0172ae] font-bold text-sm px-7 py-3.5 rounded-full hover:bg-blue-50 transition-colors"
        >
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
            <path d="M2 3a1 1 0 011-1h2.153a1 1 0 01.986.836l.74 4.435a1 1 0 01-.54 1.06l-1.548.773a11.037 11.037 0 006.105 6.105l.773-1.548a1 1 0 011.059-.54l4.435.74a1 1 0 01.836.986V17a1 1 0 01-1 1h-2C7.82 18 2 12.18 2 5V3z"/>
          </svg>
          Call 0452 188 420
        </a>
        <a
          href="tel:0721504175"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-[#f19329] hover:bg-[#d97d1a] text-white font-bold text-sm px-7 py-3.5 rounded-full transition-colors"
        >
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
            <path d="M2 3a1 1 0 011-1h2.153a1 1 0 01.986.836l.74 4.435a1 1 0 01-.54 1.06l-1.548.773a11.037 11.037 0 006.105 6.105l.773-1.548a1 1 0 011.059-.54l4.435.74a1 1 0 01.836.986V17a1 1 0 01-1 1h-2C7.82 18 2 12.18 2 5V3z"/>
          </svg>
          Call Office: 07 2150 4175
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</ServiceLayout>
